--
N5008 [dcl.init.ref]/5.1.1: a function lvalue binds directly to an lvalue
reference to function.  Every form is rejected: `void (&r)(int) = cb;' is a
"bad reference initializer", as is the global g, and the calls binding a
`void (&)(int)' or deduced `T &' parameter are conversion errors.
test_rvalue.desc covers `void (&&)(int)' and a reference through a function
alias.  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program
(-std=c++98), and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
